.TH LOXPP 1 "September 10, 2026" "loxpp 0.1.0" "Lox++ Interpreter"
.SH NAME
loxpp \- a fast, simple programming language interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loxpp
[\fIpath\fR]
.br
.B loxpp
.B \-\-check
[\fB\-\-format\fR {text|json}] \fIpath\fR
.br
.B loxpp
.B \-\-version
.br
.B loxpp
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B loxpp
interpreter runs Lox++ programs. Lox++ is a dynamically typed, single-threaded
language with classes, methods, closures, and a garbage collector.
.TP
.B loxpp \fIpath\fR
Runs the Lox++ script at \fIpath\fR.
.TP
.B loxpp
(no arguments) enters the interactive Read\-Eval\-Print Loop (REPL). The REPL
supports history (stored in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/loxpp/history " or " $HOME/.cache/loxpp/history ),
keyword completion, and line editing via the bundled isocline library.
.TP
.B loxpp \-\-check [\-\-format {text|json}] \fIpath\fR
Performs static syntax and semantic analysis on \fIpath\fR without running it.
Reports all compile\-time errors and warnings.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-format text
Human\-readable error output (default).
.TP
.B \-\-format json
Structured JSON output suitable for editor integration.
.RE
.TP
.B loxpp \-\-version
Prints the loxpp version and bundled library information.
.TP
.B loxpp \-\-help
Prints this usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Compile error when running or checking a script.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error (bad arguments or flag combination).
.TP
.B 65
Compile error (loxpp \-\-check only, exit 1 when running).
.TP
.B 70
Runtime error when running a script.
.TP
.B 74
File system error (file not found, cannot write output, etc.).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/loxpp/history
REPL command history (created on first use).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Directory for cache files. Defaults to
.IR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B HOME
User home directory (used to find the cache directory if XDG_CACHE_HOME is unset).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Lox++ project: https://github.com/txloc1909/loxpp
